{"name":"Tory Blue","hex":"#374e88","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Tory."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Tory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tory"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tory","blocks":[{"text":"A Tory is an individual who supports a political philosophy known as Toryism, based on a British version of traditionalist conservatism which upholds the established social order as it has evolved through the history of Great Britain. The Tory ethos has been summed up with the phrase \"God, King and Country\". Tories are monarchists, were historically of a high church Anglican religious heritage, and were opposed to the liberalism of the Whig party."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tory"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Royal_Oak.png/500px-Royal_Oak.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Royal_Oak.png/500px-Royal_Oak.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoyal_Oak.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg/500px-Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg/1280px-Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg/500px-Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Royalist supporters, such as the Cavaliers, were referred to as tories during the Interregnum and Restoration period in Great Britain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg/500px-John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg/1280px-John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg?utm_